patrone-shell-config (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Windows commands typed in a shell, such as ipconfig, Get-ChildItem or
    cls, in any case, now say they're invalid and name the Linux command to
    use, with the usual options where they differ. It works in bash and zsh
    for every account, new or existing: /usr/lib/command-not-found, which
    both shells run, is now Patrone's, and Ubuntu's stays beside it for
    every other command (dpkg-divert).
  * Recommends command-not-found, which sets that up for zsh.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

patrone-shell-config (0.2.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * A failed command's exit status goes on its own line under the command,
    as "✗ exit code 130", where it sat on the prompt and looked like the
    next command's. It shows once, after a command that ran, so it no longer
    stays on later prompts after an empty line. bash has it at once; an
    account's own ~/.zshrc is a copy, so zsh has it in new accounts.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:30:00 -0500

